ACE brain — third-party attributions
====================================

skills.ts adapts the "skills" architecture from OpenJarvis
(https://github.com/open-jarvis/OpenJarvis), licensed under Apache License 2.0:
self-describing capabilities that the agent discovers and invokes on demand.

ACE re-implements this pattern in TypeScript for its Claude-based brain (no
OpenJarvis code is copied verbatim; the design and skill-registry concept are
credited here). To use OpenJarvis's Python agents directly as an alternative brain
backend, run OpenJarvis as a service and have ACE's /ask call it — the Skill
interface in skills.ts is the integration seam.

